Corporate social responsibility (CSR) is the practice of taking into account the impact of business activities on society and the environment. It involves considering legal and ethical implications as well as regulatory requirements when making decisions. Companies should ensure that their operations do not cause harm to people or the environment, and strive to actively contribute to society by investing in initiatives that address social and environmental challenges. Additionally, companies should be transparent about their CSR efforts and report on their progress regularly.user

